Round 26 (2026-02-27)

What landed
- Files changed:
  - `clang/aot/emit.c`
- Added a demanded self-call lowering in `aot_emit_try_demanded_ref_call(...)`:
  - when an `APP(...REF...)` spine targets the currently emitted def (`ref_id == AOT_EMIT_DEF_ID`), generated code now calls `F_<self>(...)` directly instead of `aot_call_ref(...)`;
  - preserves the same guards as runtime dispatch:
    - depth cap check via `aot_call_depth() >= AOT_MAX_DEPTH` -> `term_new_ref(ref_id)`;
    - `AOT_CALL_DEPTH++/--` and `aot_heap_compiled_enter()/leave()` around the direct call;
  - preserves leftover-arg reapply loop exactly as before (`for (j=call_pos; j>0; j--) term_new_app(...)`), so partial/deopt behavior stays identical;
  - still gated under `STEPS_ITRS_LIM == 0`; step-limited mode keeps old structural fallback.

Why this mattered
- Compiled demanded recursion (notably `u32_fib`, `gab_takl`, `trie_bitwise`) was still paying `aot_call_ref` dispatch overhead on every recursive call.
- Heap totals already showed these paths were dispatch-bound in compiled mode, not allocation-bound.

Validation
- Build: `cd clang && clang -O2 -o main main.c`
- Tests: `./test/_all_.sh` passed.
- Deopt parity: admission canaries stayed deopt-clean where previously clean (`AOT_DEOPT total=0`), with unchanged small residual captures on `gab_takl`.
- Generated C check (`u32_fib --to-c`): demanded recursive call sites now emit direct `F_u32_fib(...)` with depth/heap guards.

