Key lessons
- There was still meaningful pure-call overhead in compiled mode even after OP2/heap optimizations.
- Removing runtime ref-table dispatch from hot recursive demanded calls can yield large wins without changing heap behavior.
- Remaining heavy cases still show dominant `WNF_DUP_NOD`/DUP pressure; this change improves dispatch cost, not duplication semantics.

Next likely steps
1) Extend direct-call emission beyond self-calls (known compiled refs) by adding safe forward declarations/prototype emission.
2) Apply the same direct-call policy in head-position REF paths where semantically equivalent.
3) Attack `WNF_DUP_NOD` with semantics-aware specialization (likely DP/MAT paths), since heap remains the dominant cost on `trie_bitwise`/`gab_takl`.
